From ed56af33b6624c0554695d5440e99b083ffa5a2c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: gugu-acp <gugu-acp@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 20:16:48 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] gugu: serve the async tasks extension on ACP v2

Why: Gugu lists a session's background commands and stops one on its own
(`_session/async_task/stop`), without stopping the turn. That lifecycle is the
AIR async tasks extension, which only an AIR client gets, and an AIR client
gets AIR's subagent form, which the v2 surface cannot send. So a v2 client
had no way to see or stop a background command: v2 has subagent sessions
(cancellable with `session/cancel`), but nothing for a background shell.

- A v2 client that is not AIR takes the extension with `_meta.asyncTasks`
  in its `initialize` capabilities. On v1 it stays AIR's, since v1 has no
  update kinds of an extension.
- The v2 surface sends the extension's updates with a leading `_`
  (`_async_task_spawned`, `_async_task_progress`, `_async_task_state_update`),
  as v2 names an extension's update kinds, and serves
  `_session/async_task/stop`.
- The "Claude is working" task of a turn that Claude Code starts on its own
  stays v1's: v2 reports that turn as foreground work.

Upstream: none yet.

Drop when: upstream offers background task control on v2.
